    "17": {
      "note": "These helpers hold navigation grouping, ordering, primary badge precedence, counts and member change facts as pure projections of the delivered outline and kept family context. Existing semantic roster ordering is separate from compact sidebar ordering. Recorded meaning is transported as the own row’s typed state/labels, never a new CHANGE_KIND, sorting weight, count or computed overall effect. An older catalogue-only listing without an admitted outline remains unbadged. OutlineRow also carries the delivered meaning state and ordered labels. memberMeaning takes the exact member’s answer from its family outline occurrence, falling back to the invariant outline entry; it never assigns the family’s labels to a member. This transports recorded judgments beside existing primary change/ordering facts and neither reclassifies change kinds nor computes a net effect.",
      "targets": [
        {
          "anchor": {
            "blob": "1e222a11645bef99a66457ef1e9ff68d8a883083",
            "content": "sha256:5917f98bf29aaf0d482c53e02c3da74df2153be2c488db6d5d7871863197ed80",
